            <ArticleTitle>Internal hernia of the transverse colon-Chilaiditi syndrome in a child.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>802-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A redundant loop of transverse colon was herniated symptomatically behind the right liver to a suprahepatic, subdiaphragmatic position in an 11-year-old girl (Chilaiditi Syndrome). Constipation from birth, partial obstruction, and recurrent severe right upper quadrant pain unresponsive to nonoperative management warranted transverse colectomy.</AbstractText>
